<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tender totals A$21.1 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tender totals A$21.1 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial paper seeped into the Australian discount securities market despite an increasingly favourable interest rate scenario with a total of A$21.1 million worth on promissory notes sold at tender.</p>
<p>Queensland-based merchant bankers Graham &amp; Co issued two parcels of 90-day paper. The A$10.0 million and A$4.1 million lots were sold at seven basis points and nine basis points respectively over the corresponding bank bill mid-rate.</p>
<p>The bank bill physical yield curve moved down and inverted further over Tuesday morning on residual positive sentiment from Monday's dealings.</p>
